# Cloudflare Workers Assets serves prerendered HTML and hashed build output
# directly (before the Worker runs), so this file — not the Worker or route
# `headers()` — controls their caching.
#
# IMPORTANT: Workers Assets *combines* (comma-joins) the headers of every rule
# whose pattern matches a request; a more specific rule does NOT override a
# broader one. So a `/*` Cache-Control would be appended to this one for every
# asset, producing a conflicting `max-age=0, ... , immutable`. We therefore only
# scope a rule to the hashed `/assets/*` output (whose filenames change every
# build, so they're safe to cache forever). HTML keeps the Workers Assets
# default `public, max-age=0, must-revalidate`, which Cloudflare still edge-caches.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
